1
00:00:41,470 --> 00:00:42,600
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:38,070 --> 00:01:43,930
[Small Town Remedy]

3
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:46,610
[Episode 2]

4
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,960
[Director's Office]

5
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:51,539
Director Chen.

6
00:01:51,590 --> 00:01:53,120
Knock the door.

7
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:55,220
Director Chen, I need a favor.

8
00:01:55,310 --> 00:01:55,950
I'm off work.

9
00:01:55,950 --> 00:01:57,610
Let's talk about it tomorrow.

10
00:01:58,710 --> 00:02:00,370
Director Chen, I need a favor.

11
00:02:02,870 --> 00:02:03,400
Go ahead.

12
00:02:05,350 --> 00:02:06,810
Liu Zhengliang's brother

13
00:02:06,950 --> 00:02:08,150
has a cerebral vascular malformation.

14
00:02:08,150 --> 00:02:09,810
The lesion's in a tricky spot.

15
00:02:09,919 --> 00:02:11,980
Director Nie can't handle this case.

16
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:14,080
So Liu is thinking
of coming to our hospital

17
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:15,360
to do the surgery for his brother.

18
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:16,120
But

19
00:02:17,750 --> 00:02:19,240
about changing

20
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,570
his practice location,

21
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:22,430
you have to find a way
to get it done for him.

22
00:02:22,430 --> 00:02:23,690
I can't help with that.

23
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:26,079
You think the hospital
is your own family's business?

24
00:02:26,079 --> 00:02:26,740
Seriously?

25
00:02:27,150 --> 00:02:28,010
Director Chen.

26
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:30,240
I know you've got your ways.

27
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:31,120
Come on, think of something.

28
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,320
Can't help with that!

29
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:34,470
Wait, you...

30
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:35,520
How about this?

31
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:37,240
We tell everyone
I'm the one performing the surgery,

32
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,310
and then he operates
on his brother instead.

33
00:02:38,310 --> 00:02:39,000
Is that okay?

34
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,240
Are you out of your mind?

35
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:41,430
You're in your thirties.

36
00:02:41,430 --> 00:02:42,079
What's going on

37
00:02:42,079 --> 00:02:43,000
in your head?

38
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:43,590
But he's my buddy.

39
00:02:43,590 --> 00:02:44,240
Is that

40
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:45,680
something a normal doctor

41
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:46,960
would say?

42
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:47,470
I...

43
00:02:47,470 --> 00:02:48,560
Your buddy...

44
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:50,310
You've got some nerve now, huh?

45
00:02:50,310 --> 00:02:51,680
Who will take the blame
if something goes wrong?

46
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:53,240
Even if I can't take it, you can!

47
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:53,870
Me?

48
00:02:53,870 --> 00:02:54,400
Yeah.

49
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:55,120
So you think

50
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:56,120
I'm living too comfortably now,

51
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:57,310
and you want to land me in jail

52
00:02:57,310 --> 00:02:58,360
eating prison food?

53
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:58,680
What are you doing?

54
00:02:58,680 --> 00:02:59,400
Aren't you my dad?

55
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:00,200
I am your dad!

56
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:01,010
Your dad...

57
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:02,750
D-Don't hit me!

58
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:05,190
Just you wait!

59
00:03:05,190 --> 00:03:06,470
I'm going to tell my mom!

60
00:03:06,470 --> 00:03:07,190
You can't!

61
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:10,960
Threatening me with your mom again.

62
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:17,060
I don't want the surgery.

63
00:03:17,150 --> 00:03:18,880
You'll die if you don't have it.

64
00:03:19,250 --> 00:03:21,010
Stop scaring me, okay?

65
00:03:21,310 --> 00:03:22,630
I'll die if I don't have it?

66
00:03:22,630 --> 00:03:23,940
I feel like I'm all better

67
00:03:23,940 --> 00:03:24,470
now.

68
00:03:24,750 --> 00:03:26,430
I can even recite ancient poems.

69
00:03:26,430 --> 00:03:27,590
"Moonlight before my bed,

70
00:03:27,590 --> 00:03:29,190
like frost upon the ground."

71
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:30,870
I can even sing.

72
00:03:31,590 --> 00:03:32,870
"Imperial Jade Wine

73
00:03:32,870 --> 00:03:34,310
costs 180 yuan per cup.

74
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:36,380
Just listen to my silver tongue."

75
00:03:37,650 --> 00:03:39,020
Hey. Hey.

76
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:40,960
Keep it down.

77
00:03:40,980 --> 00:03:42,870
We're talking about his condition here.

78
00:03:42,870 --> 00:03:44,079
I'm not scaring you.

79
00:03:44,079 --> 00:03:46,079
You're just feeling better for now.

80
00:03:46,079 --> 00:03:46,960
If we don't get rid

81
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:47,710
of the lesion completely,

82
00:03:47,710 --> 00:03:48,770
it'll bleed again,

83
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:50,470
and then you'll go see our mom.

84
00:03:50,470 --> 00:03:51,710
Don't mention our mom.

85
00:03:51,710 --> 00:03:53,130
Okay, okay.

86
00:03:53,310 --> 00:03:54,640
Don't let him get to you.

87
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:56,680
But,

88
00:03:56,750 --> 00:03:57,560
regarding your condition,

89
00:03:57,560 --> 00:03:59,190
he really wasn't scaring you.

90
00:03:59,190 --> 00:04:00,190
Just now,

91
00:04:00,590 --> 00:04:01,190
when I was talking to the doctor...

92
00:04:01,190 --> 00:04:02,680
Bro, can I use your apple?

93
00:04:03,150 --> 00:04:04,350
Don't you believe me?

94
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:06,400
Of course I believe you.

95
00:04:06,910 --> 00:04:08,510
It's a craniotomy after all.

96
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,150
At the very least, he can't be the one
operating on me, right?

97
00:04:11,150 --> 00:04:12,150
I'm not eating it!

98
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:13,820
Liu Zhengguang, look.

99
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:14,910
This is

100
00:04:14,910 --> 00:04:17,459
what your head will look like
after a craniotomy.

101
00:04:17,459 --> 00:04:18,589
This part here

102
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:19,589
is that bad thing

103
00:04:19,589 --> 00:04:20,519
in your brain.

104
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,830
It's close to the part of your brain

105
00:04:22,830 --> 00:04:24,990
that controls language function.

106
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,240
So the difficulty of this surgery

107
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:27,920
is

108
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:29,720
how to accurately and completely

109
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:30,750
remove this vascular malformation,

110
00:04:30,750 --> 00:04:31,560
which is this bad thing,

111
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:33,000
while ensuring

112
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:34,830
that your language function

113
00:04:34,830 --> 00:04:35,690
isn't damaged.

114
00:04:37,070 --> 00:04:38,240
So this time, I...

115
00:04:39,390 --> 00:04:41,000
So this time, I'm planning

116
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:42,190
to use

117
00:04:42,190 --> 00:04:43,610
an awake craniotomy.

118
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:45,010
That is to say,

119
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:47,200
during the surgery,

120
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:48,270
after opening your skull,

121
00:04:48,270 --> 00:04:49,200
I'll wake you up,

122
00:04:49,210 --> 00:04:51,409
and then the two of us will work together

123
00:04:51,630 --> 00:04:53,630
to get this bad thing

124
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:56,290
out of your head.

125
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:57,659
Do you understand?

126
00:04:59,830 --> 00:05:01,160
With my head cracked open,

127
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:02,220
I can still wake up?

128
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:04,100
Most likely, yes.

129
00:05:04,270 --> 00:05:06,070
But if there's

130
00:05:06,070 --> 00:05:08,000
bleeding or a seizure during the surgery,

131
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,390
there is still a surgical risk

132
00:05:09,390 --> 00:05:10,270
that you may never

133
00:05:10,270 --> 00:05:11,160
wake up again.

134
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:15,080
No, I don't agree.

135
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:16,870
I'd rather die

136
00:05:17,190 --> 00:05:18,160
than let you

137
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:18,960
touch my head.

138
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:22,410
Liu Zhengguang.

139
00:05:23,430 --> 00:05:24,510
Listen to me.

140
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:28,370
I've got plenty of experience
with surgeries like this.

141
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:29,240
Letting me do it for you

142
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:30,360
is better than letting some doctor
from this crappy hospital

143
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:31,310
do it for you, right?

144
00:05:31,310 --> 00:05:33,510
Stop talking. My head hurts.

145
00:05:33,510 --> 00:05:34,510
You can doubt

146
00:05:34,510 --> 00:05:35,680
our relationship,

147
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:36,680
but you can't doubt

148
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:37,740
my surgical skill.

149
00:05:38,510 --> 00:05:39,510
The quality of medical care
in Guangzhou and Shenzhen

150
00:05:39,510 --> 00:05:40,310
is far better than that

151
00:05:40,310 --> 00:05:40,950
of this crappy place.

152
00:05:40,950 --> 00:05:43,159
Stop talking. My head hurts!

153
00:05:43,390 --> 00:05:45,190
It's okay. You can talk.

154
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:46,560
I want to hear it.

155
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:48,040
What does it have to do with you?

156
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:49,480
You want to hear everything, huh?

157
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:51,680
This is the first time I've seen someone

158
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:53,370
who is so seriously ill.

159
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:54,430
I want to hear it.

160
00:05:54,430 --> 00:05:55,830
Stop talking, all of you!

161
00:05:55,830 --> 00:05:56,720
Just let me be alone

162
00:05:56,720 --> 00:05:57,830
and calm down for a bit, okay?

163
00:05:57,830 --> 00:05:58,560
Please!

164
00:05:58,560 --> 00:05:59,360
Shut up!

165
00:06:00,830 --> 00:06:02,070
He's right.

166
00:06:02,390 --> 00:06:04,050
You really are seriously ill.

167
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:11,240
You... go out and smoke a cigarette.

168
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:13,160
I don't smoke.

169
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:15,900
Can you pee?

170
00:06:18,310 --> 00:06:19,910
Or go do whatever you want!

171
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:22,060
Give us a minute alone.

172
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:25,790
Now get going.

173
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:26,460
Come on.

174
00:06:27,310 --> 00:06:28,310
Don't be anxious.

175
00:06:28,390 --> 00:06:30,120
You can't be anxious right now.

176
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:31,310
Seriously.

177
00:06:32,390 --> 00:06:33,190
Lie down.

178
00:06:35,310 --> 00:06:36,770
My head really hurts a bit.

179
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:46,510
What's wrong?

180
00:06:46,950 --> 00:06:49,409
Why aren't you going in
now that you're back?

181
00:06:51,630 --> 00:06:52,360
I'm sorry.

182
00:06:53,010 --> 00:06:54,810
I didn't get it done.

183
00:06:56,950 --> 00:06:57,560
Liu Zhengguang

184
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:59,090
won't let me operate on him.

185
00:06:59,830 --> 00:07:00,750
What did he say?

186
00:07:01,190 --> 00:07:02,190
He said he'd rather die

187
00:07:02,190 --> 00:07:03,790
than let me cut his head open.

188
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:08,870
Come on, we're both doctors.

189
00:07:08,870 --> 00:07:10,930
You should be able to understand him.

190
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:11,560
As a patient,

191
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:13,310
what he needs most right now is comfort.

192
00:07:13,310 --> 00:07:14,190
Comfort?

193
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:15,800
Can comfort cure him?

194
00:07:16,310 --> 00:07:17,160
Come on.

195
00:07:18,070 --> 00:07:19,750
Besides, he's your brother.

196
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:21,270
Try to be understanding.

197
00:07:21,270 --> 00:07:23,310
We need to figure a way out.

198
00:07:23,310 --> 00:07:24,310
What should we do?

199
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:31,410
I'll make a call.

200
00:07:34,350 --> 00:07:38,320
[Contact]

201
00:07:38,390 --> 00:07:42,750
[Fucheng No. 1 Hospital]

202
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:50,560
Hello, Jiang.

203
00:07:50,630 --> 00:07:51,270
I want to ask

204
00:07:51,270 --> 00:07:52,210
if there are any doctors in your hospital

205
00:07:52,210 --> 00:07:53,100
willing to take outside cases?

206
00:07:53,100 --> 00:07:59,000
[Fucheng No. 1 Hospital]

207
00:07:58,159 --> 00:07:59,310
What are you talking about?

208
00:07:59,310 --> 00:08:00,000
Yes.

209
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,240
I don't have many friends.

210
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:02,430
It's not your place to tell me that.

211
00:08:02,430 --> 00:08:03,760
Who do you think you are?

212
00:08:04,190 --> 00:08:04,720
Hello.

213
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:10,160
Bro,

214
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:13,180
looking for a doctor
who does outside cases?

215
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:16,630
Just tell me what the condition is,

216
00:08:16,630 --> 00:08:18,070
and I can get you any doctor you need.

217
00:08:18,070 --> 00:08:19,160
Got any from Guangdong?

218
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:20,190
Absolutely.

219
00:08:20,190 --> 00:08:21,840
This is what I do.

220
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,130
Come on, take a look.

221
00:08:25,980 --> 00:08:26,930
[Top Specialists
from Hospitals Nationwide]

222
00:08:26,930 --> 00:08:30,940
[Name: Liu Zhengliang]
[Department: Neurosurgery]

223
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:30,000
Liu Zhengliang.

224
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,010
He's from Fucheng.

225
00:08:31,010 --> 00:08:32,679
He and I grew up playing together.

226
00:08:32,679 --> 00:08:35,000
One phone call,
and the surgery's arranged.

227
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:35,929
Liu Zhengliang?

228
00:08:37,510 --> 00:08:38,909
I am Liu Zhengliang.

229
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,000
Y-You are Liu Zhengliang,

230
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,360
and you're waiting here to see a doctor?

231
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:44,900
Are you out of your mind?

232
00:08:49,030 --> 00:08:50,430
Do you still remember me?

233
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:51,870
No, I don't.

234
00:08:52,030 --> 00:08:52,960
Last night,

235
00:08:53,550 --> 00:08:55,480
I got something stuck in my windpipe.

236
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:56,440
You thought of a way

237
00:08:56,440 --> 00:08:57,910
and fished it out with a fishing net.

238
00:08:57,910 --> 00:08:58,750
Remember?

239
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,910
Which hospital are you with?

240
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:07,390
I notice none of the nurses here

241
00:09:07,390 --> 00:09:08,750
seem to know you.

242
00:09:09,510 --> 00:09:11,330
Sir, I've got things to do.

243
00:09:15,910 --> 00:09:17,200
Anyone would be on edge.

244
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:17,910
Really.

245
00:09:17,910 --> 00:09:18,480
Yeah.

246
00:09:20,150 --> 00:09:21,880
The kid's face kept going

247
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:23,720
red one minute and pale the next.

248
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:24,440
He was terrified.

249
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:26,870
It's basic survival instinct.
Fear is normal.

250
00:09:26,870 --> 00:09:27,550
Right.

251
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:29,680
We have to understand that.

252
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:30,360
Well,

253
00:09:30,670 --> 00:09:32,630
I made the call,
but I couldn't find anyone.

254
00:09:32,630 --> 00:09:33,670
I'll contact Tiantan Hospital

255
00:09:33,670 --> 00:09:35,000
and send him to Beijing.

256
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:37,000
What if his condition
gets worse on the way?

257
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,530
We can only take the gamble.

258
00:09:38,550 --> 00:09:39,270
Anyway, Liu Zhengguang

259
00:09:39,270 --> 00:09:40,960
doesn't want me to operate on him.

260
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:41,910
Let fate decide.

261
00:09:41,910 --> 00:09:42,480
No.

262
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:43,480
Your brother... You use your brother...

263
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:44,150
Well,

264
00:09:44,790 --> 00:09:47,250
Zhengguang agreed
to let you operate on him.

265
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:49,370
How did you talk him into it?

266
00:09:50,750 --> 00:09:52,010
You think I'm like you?

267
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:53,270
Waving a knife around

268
00:09:53,270 --> 00:09:55,200
and swinging it back and forth?

269
00:09:56,510 --> 00:09:57,670
Like some cold-faced mantis.

270
00:09:57,670 --> 00:09:59,070
What were you even doing?

271
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:02,290
Even if it's just a double eyelid surgery,

272
00:10:02,510 --> 00:10:04,910
it would scare him,
let alone a craniotomy.

273
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:07,630
It's useless even if he's willing now.

274
00:10:07,630 --> 00:10:09,090
I'm not qualified to do it.

275
00:10:10,870 --> 00:10:11,440
You...

276
00:10:11,910 --> 00:10:13,000
How come you're not qualified

277
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,550
all of a sudden?

278
00:10:15,150 --> 00:10:17,350
Then what were you doing there just now?

279
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:19,480
Just showing off your knife skills?

280
00:10:20,510 --> 00:10:21,670
Forget it. We don't need you anymore.

281
00:10:21,670 --> 00:10:22,750
Now I know how you got

282
00:10:22,750 --> 00:10:23,910
that top-twenty ranking.

283
00:10:23,910 --> 00:10:25,240
We don't need you, okay?

284
00:10:25,870 --> 00:10:26,670
I'll pay

285
00:10:26,910 --> 00:10:27,790
to get a top doctor here.

286
00:10:27,790 --> 00:10:29,600
-It's not about the money.
-We can't find anyone.

287
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:31,000
Why can't we find anyone?

288
00:10:31,030 --> 00:10:32,320
Someone from Hong Kong? The US?

289
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:32,750
Or...

290
00:10:32,750 --> 00:10:33,550
He might not even

291
00:10:33,550 --> 00:10:34,240
make it to Beijing,

292
00:10:34,240 --> 00:10:35,000
-let alone Hong Kong or the US.
-Then what are we supposed to do?

293
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,730
Then what are we supposed to do?

294
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:38,030
Just wait?

295
00:10:38,030 --> 00:10:39,080
The three of us just stand here
staring at each other?

296
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:40,080
Just standing here like idiots?

297
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:40,960
You're out of your depth here.

298
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:41,600
Can you just

299
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:42,500
shut up for a second?

300
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:43,840
Stop blabbering!

301
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:46,240
What the hell!

302
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:48,200
Who do you think you are?

303
00:10:48,200 --> 00:10:49,030
Are you saying that to me?

304
00:10:49,030 --> 00:10:50,480
Do you have any sense at all?

305
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:51,670
I've been looking out for him
all these years,

306
00:10:51,670 --> 00:10:52,470
you know that?

307
00:10:53,030 --> 00:10:53,870
Oh, please.

308
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:55,410
Who do you think you are?

309
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:57,270
Liu Zhengguang is my brother.

310
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:58,000
This is our family's business!

311
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,270
Is it your place to tell me about it?

312
00:10:59,270 --> 00:11:00,080
Who do you think you are?

313
00:11:00,080 --> 00:11:01,200
You're pulling that Greater Bay Area crap
on me,

314
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:01,750
huh?

315
00:11:02,510 --> 00:11:03,360
You're back in the Northeast, you know?

316
00:11:03,360 --> 00:11:03,910
What's going on?

317
00:11:03,910 --> 00:11:05,040
Don't get physical.

318
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:08,510
Chen... Chen Junnan... Chen Junnan...

319
00:11:08,510 --> 00:11:09,570
What are you doing?

320
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:11,360
You're back in the Northeast.

321
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:12,360
Nobody gets to act tough here,

322
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:13,080
got it?

323
00:11:13,550 --> 00:11:14,480
I'm telling you,

324
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:16,050
if you keep defying me,

325
00:11:16,050 --> 00:11:17,910
I'll knock you out with one punch!

326
00:11:19,150 --> 00:11:20,370
Call the police!

327
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:22,040
Liu Zhengguang is so unlucky

328
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:23,480
to have a brother like you.

329
00:11:23,480 --> 00:11:24,240
You idiot!

330
00:11:28,030 --> 00:11:28,910
You're so big and tall,

331
00:11:28,910 --> 00:11:30,770
and you can't even push a girl off?

332
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:31,600
You try it!

333
00:11:32,670 --> 00:11:33,730
This crappy place.

334
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:35,790
There are all kinds of savages here.

335
00:11:35,790 --> 00:11:37,150
What's wrong with this place?

336
00:11:37,150 --> 00:11:38,750
Didn't this place raise you?

337
00:11:38,910 --> 00:11:40,000
Full of savages.

338
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,440
Well, Dr. Chen,

339
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:45,320
I brought a box of tea for each of you,

340
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:46,780
just to show my gratitude.

341
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,250
I'll leave it to you.

342
00:11:48,870 --> 00:11:49,600
Don't go.

343
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:50,840
That's very kind of you,

344
00:11:50,840 --> 00:11:51,960
but there are rules at our hospital.

345
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:52,870
We can't take this.

346
00:11:52,870 --> 00:11:53,790
It's not a big gift.

347
00:11:53,790 --> 00:11:54,440
No, no, no.

348
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:55,910
It's just a little token of appreciation
from me.

349
00:11:55,910 --> 00:11:56,670
There are rules.

350
00:11:56,670 --> 00:11:57,550
Look, so many people are watching.

351
00:11:57,550 --> 00:11:58,000
Hold it for me for a second.

352
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,360
I need to tie my shoelace.

353
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:01,080
Everyone is staring.

354
00:12:02,750 --> 00:12:03,750
Sir, I really can't take it.

355
00:12:03,750 --> 00:12:04,320
Don't...

356
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:06,150
It's already in your hands.

357
00:12:06,150 --> 00:12:06,550
Just take it.

358
00:12:06,550 --> 00:12:07,480
No, no, no. Take it back.

359
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:08,550
Let's not keep passing it back and forth.

360
00:12:08,550 --> 00:12:09,960
Sir, take it back.

361
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:11,510
Really. So many eyes are on us.

362
00:12:11,510 --> 00:12:12,600
I can't take anything from you.

363
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:13,530
President Long.

364
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:17,120
President Long.

365
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:19,600
Isn't this Chen Kai?

366
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:20,150
Yes.

367
00:12:20,150 --> 00:12:21,080
Long time no see.

368
00:12:21,550 --> 00:12:22,870
You know each other, Dad?

369
00:12:22,870 --> 00:12:23,450
What?

370
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:25,840
The former president
of the Second Hospital.

371
00:12:25,840 --> 00:12:26,970
My former superior.

372
00:12:28,120 --> 00:12:28,920
You look well.

373
00:12:29,750 --> 00:12:30,550
This is my son,

374
00:12:30,790 --> 00:12:31,600
Chen Junnan.

375
00:12:31,870 --> 00:12:32,930
Hello, President.

376
00:12:33,630 --> 00:12:35,030
Don't call me President.

377
00:12:35,150 --> 00:12:35,960
Call me Uncle.

378
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:37,040
Hello, Uncle.

379
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:38,120
I...

380
00:12:38,120 --> 00:12:39,120
This...

381
00:12:39,790 --> 00:12:40,590
You look well.

382
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:42,390
I'm not at the Second Hospital anymore.

383
00:12:42,390 --> 00:12:43,720
I'm back at Xiaoximen Hospital.

384
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:44,390
I know.

385
00:12:44,390 --> 00:12:45,320
You always go

386
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:46,670
wherever you're needed the most.

387
00:12:46,670 --> 00:12:47,390
What's up?

388
00:12:47,390 --> 00:12:48,910
Why are you here today?

389
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:50,960
Don't mention it.

390
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:52,600
I ate something wrong yesterday,

391
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:54,260
and it went down the windpipe.

392
00:12:54,750 --> 00:12:56,390
Your son saved me.

393
00:12:56,390 --> 00:12:57,440
I owe your son

394
00:12:58,240 --> 00:12:59,270
a huge favor.

395
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:00,480
Long time no see.

396
00:13:00,910 --> 00:13:01,810
Let's have a drink.

397
00:13:01,810 --> 00:13:02,410
Chen.

398
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:03,910
To be honest, I've quit drinking.

399
00:13:03,910 --> 00:13:04,840
What do you mean you've quit drinking?

400
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:06,240
-I really have.
-It's been a long time.

401
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:06,840
Well,

402
00:13:07,360 --> 00:13:08,240
here's a box of tea for your dad.

403
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:09,150
I'll take this box back.

404
00:13:09,150 --> 00:13:10,150
No need. No need.

405
00:13:10,150 --> 00:13:10,510
Just take it.

406
00:13:10,510 --> 00:13:11,200
No, no, no.

407
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:11,870
You...

408
00:13:12,550 --> 00:13:13,270
Let's go.

409
00:13:13,270 --> 00:13:13,870
Let's have a drink.

410
00:13:13,870 --> 00:13:14,510
I really don't drink anymore.

411
00:13:14,510 --> 00:13:15,510
Then I'll go back.

412
00:13:15,510 --> 00:13:16,270
No, no, no.

413
00:13:16,270 --> 00:13:17,080
We don't get to see each other often.

414
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:17,510
Uncle.

415
00:13:17,870 --> 00:13:20,360
Didn't you say

416
00:13:20,750 --> 00:13:22,840
y-you owe me a favor?

417
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:23,790
So?

418
00:13:26,790 --> 00:13:28,050
Can you pay it back now?

419
00:13:29,790 --> 00:13:30,600
One minute you say you'll do it,

420
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:31,320
and the next you say you won't.

421
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:32,650
Are you messing with me?

422
00:13:33,510 --> 00:13:34,910
There's no other way now.

423
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:36,450
This is the only way.

424
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:39,200
Didn't you say going to Beijing

425
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:40,320
carries even greater risks?

426
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:41,120
That's right.

427
00:13:41,790 --> 00:13:42,790
On the way there, your condition

428
00:13:42,790 --> 00:13:44,250
can very likely get worse.

429
00:13:51,630 --> 00:13:52,560
Liu Zhengliang.

430
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:54,270
I...

431
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:56,960
If anything happens to me,

432
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:00,210
you have to find Mom.

433
00:14:01,670 --> 00:14:02,530
Did you hear me?

434
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:06,000
Rest assured.

435
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:08,910
Just focus on yourself.

436
00:14:16,630 --> 00:14:18,290
Actually, I know everything.

437
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:22,870
Say something.

438
00:14:22,870 --> 00:14:23,630
Know what?

439
00:14:24,870 --> 00:14:27,000
I know I'm not Mom's biological child.

440
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,120
I was adopted.

441
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:35,630
I saw with my own eyes

442
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:38,080
that Mom was pregnant with you
and gave birth to you.

443
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:39,150
How could you possibly be adopted?

444
00:14:39,150 --> 00:14:40,360
What are you thinking?

445
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:41,720
People at our age

446
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:42,980
are all only children.

447
00:14:43,030 --> 00:14:43,910
When I was in school,

448
00:14:43,910 --> 00:14:45,270
all my classmates were only children.

449
00:14:45,270 --> 00:14:46,320
None of them had siblings.

450
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:46,790
How do you explain that?

451
00:14:46,790 --> 00:14:48,390
You were born over the quota.

452
00:14:49,270 --> 00:14:51,080
Dad even paid a fine for you.

453
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:55,300
He passed away right after paying it.

454
00:14:57,550 --> 00:14:59,870
Neat story. Sounds convincing.

455
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:02,360
Unfortunately, I have solid proof.

456
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:04,240
Mom sent you to the South.

457
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:05,670
For all these years,
she had no one by her side,

458
00:15:05,670 --> 00:15:07,030
so she chose me.

459
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:09,240
She adopted me as your replacement.

460
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:10,360
For all these years,

461
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:11,670
I just couldn't figure it out.

462
00:15:11,670 --> 00:15:12,910
Mom talked about you every day.

463
00:15:12,910 --> 00:15:14,310
She missed you every day.

464
00:15:14,550 --> 00:15:15,550
I was by her side,

465
00:15:15,550 --> 00:15:16,480
keeping her company every day,

466
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:17,810
but she just ignored me!

467
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,660
Doesn't that say everything?

468
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:23,670
I know

469
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:27,870
it wasn't easy for Mom
to raise me all these years.

470
00:15:27,870 --> 00:15:28,600
No matter

471
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:30,030
whether I'm her biological son or not,
I have to accept it.

472
00:15:30,030 --> 00:15:31,510
I still recognize her as my mom,

473
00:15:31,510 --> 00:15:33,170
and I have to do my duty as a son.

474
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:35,080
I need

475
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:36,120
to fulfill every son's obligation

476
00:15:36,120 --> 00:15:37,150
on your behalf.

477
00:15:39,270 --> 00:15:40,200
Liu Zhengguang,

478
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:42,320
sometimes I really wish

479
00:15:42,320 --> 00:15:43,910
we weren't real brothers.

480
00:15:43,910 --> 00:15:46,270
See? You're telling the truth now.

481
00:15:46,270 --> 00:15:47,080
You're such an idiot.

482
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:48,610
If you'd said so earlier...

483
00:15:49,550 --> 00:15:50,440
I've got a way.

484
00:15:51,020 --> 00:15:58,370
[The Old Captain]

485
00:15:54,550 --> 00:15:55,120
Listen.

486
00:15:56,670 --> 00:15:57,390
You sign an employment contract

487
00:15:57,390 --> 00:15:58,440
with Xiaoximen Hospital

488
00:15:58,440 --> 00:15:59,510
where I work.

489
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:02,920
[Scallops with Vermicelli—Dig In!]

490
00:16:02,150 --> 00:16:03,670
I'll use my own methods

491
00:16:04,280 --> 00:16:06,370
♪ The sun's already high
and I'm just getting downstairs ♪

492
00:16:04,320 --> 00:16:05,630
to get you registered

493
00:16:05,630 --> 00:16:06,750
as quickly as possible,

494
00:16:06,390 --> 00:16:08,700
♪ My hair is a flattened mess,
like a bird's nest ♪

495
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:09,360
so you can get your medical license.

496
00:16:09,680 --> 00:16:11,520
♪ There is nothing much in my pockets ♪

497
00:16:11,890 --> 00:16:13,910
♪ I still sway a little as I walk ♪

498
00:16:14,610 --> 00:16:15,770
♪ A buddy at the door calls out to me ♪

499
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:17,040
♪ Where are you off to? ♪

500
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:18,450
♪ I say I don't know yet ♪

501
00:16:18,710 --> 00:16:19,770
♪ Just gonna head on forward ♪

502
00:16:20,030 --> 00:16:22,410
♪ And see where I end up ♪

503
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:21,670
But I have a few questions

504
00:16:21,670 --> 00:16:22,480
for you.

505
00:16:22,790 --> 00:16:24,600
♪ Anyway, there isn't much to do
at home ♪

506
00:16:24,440 --> 00:16:25,120
Go ahead.

507
00:16:26,870 --> 00:16:27,720
Why were you

508
00:16:29,870 --> 00:16:31,870
fired from your previous hospital?

509
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:34,150
Because I did

510
00:16:34,150 --> 00:16:36,030
an outside surgery that went very badly.

511
00:16:36,030 --> 00:16:37,090
Whose fault was it?

512
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:37,840
Mine.

513
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:40,150
After you finish the surgery
for your brother,

514
00:16:40,150 --> 00:16:41,270
are you willing to stay at our hospital?

515
00:16:41,270 --> 00:16:42,030
No.

516
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:44,660
What are you doing?

517
00:16:45,510 --> 00:16:48,240
We're here to get something done.
Talk properly.

518
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:50,550
After the surgery, I'm leaving.

519
00:16:50,550 --> 00:16:52,150
I have to go back to the South.

520
00:16:54,250 --> 00:16:55,240
Surgical skills,

521
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:56,640
patient communication,

522
00:16:56,790 --> 00:16:57,920
clinical teaching,

523
00:16:58,360 --> 00:16:59,320
and research papers.

524
00:16:59,320 --> 00:17:00,240
On a scale of 1 to 10
for these five categories,

525
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:01,840
how would you rate yourself?

526
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:03,630
Eight. Nine.

527
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:06,910
Three. Seven. Eight.

528
00:17:07,630 --> 00:17:09,630
So you have trouble communicating?

529
00:17:09,750 --> 00:17:10,680
I don't think so,

530
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:11,589
but my former colleagues

531
00:17:11,589 --> 00:17:12,390
all think I do.

532
00:17:13,790 --> 00:17:15,480
You trust your colleagues' judgment

533
00:17:15,480 --> 00:17:16,540
more than your own?

534
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:18,880
I just think

535
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:19,920
patients and their families

536
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:21,240
sometimes don't understand
what I'm saying.

537
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:24,440
Doesn't that still show
you have trouble communicating?

538
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:27,680
So you do or you don't?

539
00:17:29,270 --> 00:17:29,720
I do.

540
00:17:34,550 --> 00:17:35,640
Last question.

541
00:17:36,350 --> 00:17:37,550
Why should I help you?

542
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:38,550
Uncle Long,

543
00:17:38,550 --> 00:17:39,920
don't you owe me a favor?

544
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:41,200
When it's official business,

545
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:42,530
call me President Long.

546
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:44,640
I'm willing to sit down

547
00:17:44,640 --> 00:17:45,700
and give you ideas.

548
00:17:45,790 --> 00:17:47,720
That favor is basically repaid.

549
00:17:49,480 --> 00:17:50,740
Well, President Long,

550
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:53,200
it seems
that favor doesn't count for much.

551
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:54,510
Special cases need special treatment.

552
00:17:54,510 --> 00:17:57,480
We've got to count both the onboarding
and the offboarding.

553
00:17:57,480 --> 00:17:58,310
Understood.

554
00:17:59,030 --> 00:18:00,750
How about this, President Long?

555
00:18:00,750 --> 00:18:02,030
If you have any other conditions,

556
00:18:02,030 --> 00:18:02,830
just say them.

557
00:18:03,920 --> 00:18:04,880
There will be an extra fee.

558
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:05,440
How much?

559
00:18:05,750 --> 00:18:06,310
20,000.

560
00:18:07,240 --> 00:18:08,400
It's not for me personally.

561
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:10,440
You donate it directly to the hospital.

562
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:11,750
Your brother's medical expenses

563
00:18:11,750 --> 00:18:13,070
will be calculated separately.

564
00:18:13,070 --> 00:18:14,330
I can issue an invoice.

565
00:18:14,350 --> 00:18:15,680
Uncle Long, this is robbery!

566
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:16,480
Screw you.

567
00:18:18,480 --> 00:18:19,000
Okay.

568
00:18:19,650 --> 00:18:20,850
Okay?

569
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:21,720
You're broke.

570
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:22,510
Where are you gonna get so much money?

571
00:18:22,510 --> 00:18:23,480
How can you say okay?

572
00:18:23,480 --> 00:18:24,830
My mom's will says

573
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:25,960
that she had some savings.

574
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:27,400
Aren't you going to discuss it
with your brother?

575
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:28,880
What's there to discuss with him?

576
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:31,540
The money will be used
for his treatment anyway.

577
00:18:37,550 --> 00:18:38,310
Uncle Long, here's the thing.

578
00:18:38,310 --> 00:18:39,370
This friend of mine

579
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:41,750
doesn't stay in Fucheng much.

580
00:18:41,750 --> 00:18:43,830
He doesn't know the situation here.

581
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:45,160
If I may ask,

582
00:18:45,550 --> 00:18:46,350
are the medical facilities

583
00:18:46,350 --> 00:18:47,550
at Xiaoximen Hospital

584
00:18:47,550 --> 00:18:48,410
up to standard?

585
00:18:49,030 --> 00:18:51,430
Do you have a qualified anesthesiologist?

586
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:57,160
I can bring in

587
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:58,240
the best anesthesiologist

588
00:18:58,240 --> 00:18:59,240
from the city.

589
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:00,750
As for the equipment,

590
00:19:00,750 --> 00:19:01,510
you can come to the hospital
tomorrow morning

591
00:19:01,510 --> 00:19:02,750
and see for yourself.

592
00:19:04,270 --> 00:19:05,510
If you're satisfied,

593
00:19:05,590 --> 00:19:06,790
we'll sign the contract tomorrow noon,

594
00:19:06,790 --> 00:19:09,390
and the surgery
will be the day after tomorrow.

595
00:19:09,570 --> 00:19:10,220
♪ Just wandering around ♪

596
00:19:10,750 --> 00:19:11,580
♪ Just wandering around ♪

597
00:19:11,910 --> 00:19:14,480
♪ This town is just so small ♪

598
00:19:13,470 --> 00:19:14,750
Alright, let's do that.

599
00:19:14,750 --> 00:19:15,510
Pleasure working with you.

600
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:16,980
♪ Running into a former classmate
on the east side ♪

601
00:19:17,150 --> 00:19:18,900
♪ Running into my uncle on the west side ♪

602
00:19:19,090 --> 00:19:20,240
♪ What're you looking at? ♪

603
00:19:19,480 --> 00:19:20,960
I... I'll get this. I'll get this.

604
00:19:20,510 --> 00:19:21,830
♪ Quit staring ♪

605
00:19:22,260 --> 00:19:24,590
♪ Staring won't change a thing ♪

606
00:19:25,110 --> 00:19:25,860
♪ Bored out of my mind ♪

607
00:19:26,110 --> 00:19:27,340
♪ I have a couple of drinks ♪

608
00:19:27,540 --> 00:19:30,500
♪ First one to pass out is a loser ♪

609
00:19:28,110 --> 00:19:29,590
Is he reliable?

610
00:19:30,750 --> 00:19:32,270
It's our only shot.

611
00:19:30,950 --> 00:19:32,060
♪ Just wandering around ♪

612
00:19:32,400 --> 00:19:33,550
We have to try.

613
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:33,170
♪ Just wandering around ♪

614
00:19:33,570 --> 00:19:36,110
♪ Young people
don't make that many plans ♪

615
00:19:34,030 --> 00:19:35,960
He's Chen Kai's old buddy.

616
00:19:36,310 --> 00:19:38,340
♪ The sun's pretty nice today ♪

617
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:38,330
Come on, eat something.

618
00:19:38,810 --> 00:19:41,360
♪ Let's go out and not waste the day ♪

619
00:19:40,510 --> 00:19:41,270
Wait, that one's burnt.

620
00:19:41,270 --> 00:19:41,820
Have this one.

621
00:19:41,820 --> 00:19:42,360
♪ Let's go ♪

622
00:19:43,060 --> 00:19:43,930
♪ Where are you going? ♪

623
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:44,160
I'm starving.

624
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:45,140
♪ Don't know ♪

625
00:19:45,240 --> 00:19:45,960
Is it good?

626
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:46,470
♪ Then why're you going? ♪

627
00:19:47,510 --> 00:19:48,920
I haven't eaten yet.

628
00:19:47,850 --> 00:19:49,110
♪ Just wandering around ♪

629
00:19:50,270 --> 00:19:51,070
Try it.

630
00:19:52,160 --> 00:19:58,820
[Mic King Zone] [Starry Night]

631
00:20:01,510 --> 00:20:03,970
That kid's research papers
are pretty good.

632
00:20:05,110 --> 00:20:06,140
Jianguo,

633
00:20:06,270 --> 00:20:08,200
can you ask around about a guy for me?

634
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:10,000
His name is Liu Zhengliang.

635
00:20:11,550 --> 00:20:12,200
Male.

636
00:20:12,510 --> 00:20:13,830
Age...

637
00:20:14,300 --> 00:20:16,160
Probably in his early thirties.

638
00:20:17,830 --> 00:20:20,200
He used to w-work

639
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:21,460
at S-Shenya Hospital.

640
00:20:22,240 --> 00:20:23,220
Long, then

641
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:25,010
what do you want to know?

642
00:20:26,270 --> 00:20:27,730
I want to know everything,

643
00:20:28,270 --> 00:20:30,030
but the most important thing

644
00:20:30,030 --> 00:20:31,890
is his professional competence.

645
00:21:02,160 --> 00:21:03,510
I'm the kid's uncle.

646
00:21:03,830 --> 00:21:05,290
We came to Beijing specifically for this.

647
00:21:05,290 --> 00:21:06,790
Doctor, please take a look.

648
00:21:06,790 --> 00:21:08,070
This kid's illness

649
00:21:08,070 --> 00:21:09,200
is very rare.

650
00:21:09,280 --> 00:21:11,550
It's a type
of post-traumatic stress disorder.

651
00:21:09,570 --> 00:21:13,920
[Beijing]

652
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:13,270
So far,

653
00:21:13,270 --> 00:21:14,030
there is no confirmed

654
00:21:14,030 --> 00:21:15,440
effective treatment.

655
00:21:18,350 --> 00:21:18,960
Doctor,

656
00:21:19,550 --> 00:21:21,590
is there any medicine for this?

657
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:24,720
I've heard about qigong,

658
00:21:25,310 --> 00:21:26,110
hypnosis and stuff.

659
00:21:26,110 --> 00:21:26,840
Do they work?

660
00:21:27,790 --> 00:21:30,110
Don't go chasing
all these random treatments.

661
00:21:30,110 --> 00:21:31,790
You'll end up hurting the kid.

662
00:21:32,070 --> 00:21:32,920
You may as well

663
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:34,920
change the environment for the kid.

664
00:21:35,750 --> 00:21:37,310
Changing the environment will help?

665
00:21:37,310 --> 00:21:37,880
Yes.

666
00:21:44,880 --> 00:21:47,310
Mom, I don't want to go to Guangzhou.

667
00:21:47,310 --> 00:21:49,510
You're going whether you want to or not.

668
00:21:50,350 --> 00:21:51,680
See this jacket?

669
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:52,750
Don't wash it.

670
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:55,680
I sewed 100 yuan and a phone number

671
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:56,720
in the pocket.

672
00:21:58,550 --> 00:22:00,210
You must listen to your uncle.

673
00:22:00,680 --> 00:22:02,270
If there's something urgent,

674
00:22:02,270 --> 00:22:04,440
use the money to call me.

675
00:22:04,790 --> 00:22:05,650
I'll go see you.

676
00:22:09,160 --> 00:22:09,680
Mom,

677
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:11,920
are you sending me away

678
00:22:12,350 --> 00:22:14,550
because you have my little brother now?

679
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:36,640
I want you to stay here

680
00:22:36,640 --> 00:22:37,900
more than anyone else.

681
00:22:38,830 --> 00:22:40,000
But you can't just hide at home

682
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:41,480
every time winter comes.

683
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:44,310
If you can't stay in the Northeast,

684
00:22:44,310 --> 00:22:45,910
then move to somewhere else.

685
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:48,480
You have to live well.

686
00:22:54,350 --> 00:22:55,750
The snow in the Northeast

687
00:22:58,590 --> 00:22:59,790
is too heavy.

688
00:23:02,680 --> 00:23:04,310
The winter is too long.

689
00:23:22,590 --> 00:23:23,340
[Construction Area — No Climbing Over]

690
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:50,220
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

691
00:23:51,310 --> 00:23:52,570
You're Dr. Liu, right?

692
00:23:53,590 --> 00:23:55,030
I'm Che Mingming
from Neurosurgical Department.

693
00:23:55,030 --> 00:23:56,440
The president sent me to pick you up.

694
00:23:56,440 --> 00:23:57,300
Just follow me.

695
00:24:00,960 --> 00:24:01,550
What's wrong?

696
00:24:01,550 --> 00:24:02,610
You're not Dr. Liu?

697
00:24:04,110 --> 00:24:04,830
I am.

698
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:06,780
Then follow me.

699
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:11,880
[West Gate]

700
00:24:18,310 --> 00:24:19,920
I heard you're also a local.

701
00:24:20,550 --> 00:24:22,550
Haven't been back for years, right?

702
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:24,730
Things have changed a lot here.

703
00:24:25,640 --> 00:24:26,200
This way.

704
00:24:26,710 --> 00:24:32,940
[Patient-Centered, Quality-Focused]

705
00:24:31,110 --> 00:24:32,270
When you came just now,

706
00:24:32,270 --> 00:24:33,510
you probably saw it too.

707
00:24:33,510 --> 00:24:35,640
There are commercial streets
all around us.

708
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:36,440
That's because

709
00:24:36,440 --> 00:24:37,590
we exchanged the old buildings
facing the street

710
00:24:37,590 --> 00:24:38,160
with the builders

711
00:24:38,160 --> 00:24:39,350
who construct buildings

712
00:24:38,810 --> 00:24:42,290
[Clinical Laboratory]
[Radiology Department]

713
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:41,210
to rent out as storefronts.

714
00:24:41,990 --> 00:24:43,580
It was all our president's idea.

715
00:24:42,410 --> 00:24:48,250
[Outpatient Hall]

716
00:24:45,110 --> 00:24:46,070
When the new buildings are done,

717
00:24:46,070 --> 00:24:48,340
the president will get two more buildings
for free.

718
00:24:48,340 --> 00:24:51,840
[Pharmacy]

719
00:24:48,480 --> 00:24:49,550
This place doesn't quite comply

720
00:24:49,550 --> 00:24:52,210
with the regulations
for medical land, does it?

721
00:24:52,590 --> 00:24:53,680
What's the big deal?

722
00:24:53,680 --> 00:24:55,110
Our president has strong connections.

723
00:24:54,870 --> 00:25:00,500
[Treating patients with skill
and compassion]

724
00:24:57,920 --> 00:24:59,000
There are two more doors here.

725
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:00,330
They're all connected.

726
00:25:00,590 --> 00:25:01,520
Watch your step.

727
00:25:02,590 --> 00:25:05,110
The first and third floors here
are outpatient clinics.

728
00:25:05,110 --> 00:25:07,510
Over there on the first floor
is the emergency department.

729
00:25:07,510 --> 00:25:10,240
Further down are logistics
and the cafeteria.

730
00:25:14,270 --> 00:25:15,640
Surgery is on the second floor.

731
00:25:15,640 --> 00:25:17,700
Further up are research and offices.

732
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:21,220
The inpatient department
is in the the building next door.

733
00:25:24,830 --> 00:25:26,680
These devices are all the latest.

734
00:25:26,680 --> 00:25:27,510
How about it?

735
00:25:27,680 --> 00:25:28,270
Not worse than those big hospitals

736
00:25:28,270 --> 00:25:30,050
in Shenzhen, right?

737
00:25:34,720 --> 00:25:36,320
I really didn't expect this.

738
00:25:36,640 --> 00:25:37,640
Such an inconspicuous hospital

739
00:25:37,640 --> 00:25:39,160
from the outside

740
00:25:40,110 --> 00:25:41,510
has quite reliable operating rooms.

741
00:25:41,510 --> 00:25:42,880
Our president has strong connections.

742
00:25:42,880 --> 00:25:45,350
These are all obtained
through internal channels.

743
00:25:45,350 --> 00:25:45,830
Let's go.

744
00:25:45,830 --> 00:25:46,640
I'll take you to the ICU

745
00:25:46,640 --> 00:25:47,350
for a walk.

746
00:25:48,640 --> 00:25:50,120
I'm here to do surgery,

747
00:25:50,200 --> 00:25:51,530
not to visit.

748
00:25:51,790 --> 00:25:53,070
What's the harm in taking a look?

749
00:25:53,070 --> 00:25:54,270
You're already here.

750
00:25:54,510 --> 00:25:55,790
Our president told me

751
00:25:56,030 --> 00:25:57,030
that I must

752
00:25:57,030 --> 00:25:58,240
show you

753
00:25:58,240 --> 00:26:00,680
the hardware capabilities
of our Xiaoximen Hospital.

754
00:26:00,680 --> 00:26:01,440
Let's go.

755
00:26:07,740 --> 00:26:13,200
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

756
00:26:10,070 --> 00:26:12,110
You don't even have money
to build a building.

757
00:26:12,110 --> 00:26:14,200
Where did you get the money to buy these?

758
00:26:14,200 --> 00:26:15,000
Loans.

759
00:26:15,830 --> 00:26:16,590
Loans?

760
00:26:16,960 --> 00:26:17,790
Can you pay them back?

761
00:26:17,670 --> 00:26:22,710
[Keep the ward clean and tidy]

762
00:26:18,350 --> 00:26:19,480
So what if we can't?

763
00:26:19,830 --> 00:26:22,030
Our president has strong connections.

764
00:26:25,750 --> 00:26:27,480
Comrade Liu, how is it?

765
00:26:26,420 --> 00:26:30,210
[No smoking] [Keep quiet]

766
00:26:27,480 --> 00:26:28,540
Are you satisfied?

767
00:26:29,400 --> 00:26:30,530
Yes, I'm satisfied.

768
00:26:33,400 --> 00:26:35,400
The contract is ready. Just sign it.

769
00:26:37,480 --> 00:26:38,400
Sign it here?

770
00:26:38,880 --> 00:26:39,350
Then...

771
00:26:41,480 --> 00:26:42,750
Then sign it on my back.

772
00:26:53,680 --> 00:26:55,280
I need to read this contract.

773
00:26:55,590 --> 00:26:57,070
I was just afraid you were in a hurry.

774
00:26:57,070 --> 00:26:58,400
There's no rush for now.

775
00:26:58,960 --> 00:27:00,830
As if I could trick him.

776
00:27:03,200 --> 00:27:04,200
Then take your time

777
00:27:04,200 --> 00:27:04,880
and read it.

778
00:27:05,400 --> 00:27:06,860
I'm going to play mahjong.

779
00:27:07,240 --> 00:27:09,640
You're playing mahjong again, President?

780
00:27:09,640 --> 00:27:10,240
Once you start playing,

781
00:27:10,240 --> 00:27:11,510
it'll be a whole day and night.

782
00:27:11,220 --> 00:27:14,600
[To Building 2]

783
00:27:11,510 --> 00:27:12,680
Then who will stamp

784
00:27:12,680 --> 00:27:13,810
Dr. Liu's contract?

785
00:27:13,920 --> 00:27:15,650
He doesn't seem to be in a hurry.

786
00:27:15,680 --> 00:27:18,210
Isn't the patient arriving
in the afternoon?

787
00:27:18,310 --> 00:27:20,680
Did you contact that anesthesiologist?

788
00:27:21,790 --> 00:27:24,400
I'll count down three numbers,
and he'll definitely come over.

789
00:27:24,400 --> 00:27:25,110
Three...

790
00:27:25,640 --> 00:27:26,160
Two...

791
00:27:27,070 --> 00:27:27,680
One.

792
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:29,660
Did he move?

793
00:27:32,790 --> 00:27:33,480
No.

794
00:27:34,770 --> 00:27:37,830
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

795
00:27:38,640 --> 00:27:40,000
This guy is too calm.

796
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:41,350
He's just like me.

797
00:27:53,960 --> 00:27:54,720
What should we do?

798
00:27:54,720 --> 00:27:56,380
He's reading very carefully.

799
00:28:09,350 --> 00:28:10,640
I brought the bankbook.

800
00:28:10,640 --> 00:28:11,510
Where do I pay?

801
00:28:11,880 --> 00:28:13,200
No rush to pay.

802
00:28:13,920 --> 00:28:15,830
How do you feel about the contract?

803
00:28:15,830 --> 00:28:17,290
Your contract is not good.

804
00:28:17,920 --> 00:28:20,580
The term is too long,
and the penalty is too high.

805
00:28:21,160 --> 00:28:22,070
This is different
from what we talked about

806
00:28:22,070 --> 00:28:22,730
yesterday.

807
00:28:25,960 --> 00:28:26,680
Okay.

808
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:29,680
Since we hit it off right away,

809
00:28:30,590 --> 00:28:32,590
I'll just collect the medical fees.

810
00:28:33,110 --> 00:28:34,110
And I won't charge you

811
00:28:34,110 --> 00:28:35,040
any extra money.

812
00:28:38,640 --> 00:28:40,440
Weren't you fired from your job?

813
00:28:41,200 --> 00:28:42,600
With such a big incident,

814
00:28:43,160 --> 00:28:44,200
in the short term,

815
00:28:44,200 --> 00:28:46,330
no hospital in Shenzhen will hire you.

816
00:28:46,550 --> 00:28:48,350
You might as well just stay here.

817
00:28:50,640 --> 00:28:51,770
That's impossible.

818
00:28:54,720 --> 00:28:55,590
Don't go.

819
00:28:55,790 --> 00:28:57,550
We just hit it off right away.

820
00:28:57,830 --> 00:28:58,960
Since you're here, you might as well stay.

821
00:28:58,960 --> 00:28:59,960
We agreed.

822
00:29:00,110 --> 00:29:02,440
Pay the money and do the job,
nothing else.

823
00:29:04,440 --> 00:29:06,370
I don't want money. I just want you.

824
00:29:06,440 --> 00:29:07,680
If you don't stay,

825
00:29:07,680 --> 00:29:08,550
things won't be easy to handle.

826
00:29:08,550 --> 00:29:11,550
So you're the one responsible
for my brother's death.

827
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:12,750
Your brother is sick.

828
00:29:12,750 --> 00:29:13,440
What does that have to do with me?

829
00:29:13,440 --> 00:29:14,240
It didn't before,

830
00:29:14,240 --> 00:29:14,880
but it does now.

831
00:29:14,880 --> 00:29:15,750
What does it...

832
00:29:16,500 --> 00:29:18,160
What does it have to do with me?

833
00:29:19,240 --> 00:29:20,510
I run a hospital.

834
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:22,800
Would I be afraid of dead people?

835
00:29:24,640 --> 00:29:25,840
That is your brother.

836
00:29:26,270 --> 00:29:27,800
You figure it out yourself.

837
00:29:29,550 --> 00:29:31,240
Why are you getting so anxious?

838
00:29:31,240 --> 00:29:31,900
President.

839
00:29:33,400 --> 00:29:33,930
Three...

840
00:29:34,720 --> 00:29:35,310
Two...

841
00:29:35,400 --> 00:29:35,960
Wait.

842
00:29:35,960 --> 00:29:36,540
One.

843
00:29:45,550 --> 00:29:47,880
What's the situation with the surgery?

844
00:29:47,880 --> 00:29:49,680
How did your brother arrange it?

845
00:29:49,880 --> 00:29:50,720
I don't know.

846
00:29:51,960 --> 00:29:53,030
He just told me

847
00:29:53,030 --> 00:29:54,030
to wait for news.

848
00:29:54,680 --> 00:29:55,310
Let me tell you,

849
00:29:55,310 --> 00:29:56,400
tonight,

850
00:29:56,400 --> 00:29:57,510
you need to go to bed early,

851
00:29:57,510 --> 00:29:58,200
you know?

852
00:29:58,550 --> 00:29:59,950
It'll be fine after this.

853
00:30:00,510 --> 00:30:01,310
My brother...

854
00:30:03,510 --> 00:30:04,510
Let me tell you, sis.

855
00:30:04,510 --> 00:30:05,640
He is cold-blooded.

856
00:30:07,960 --> 00:30:09,620
He never cares if I live or die.

857
00:30:11,070 --> 00:30:13,240
He never cared about me and my mom.

858
00:30:13,310 --> 00:30:14,930
Don't think like that.

859
00:30:15,200 --> 00:30:16,550
Besides your mom,

860
00:30:16,750 --> 00:30:18,880
isn't your brother the closest to you?

861
00:30:20,270 --> 00:30:22,000
How could he bear to ignore you?

862
00:30:22,920 --> 00:30:24,160
Go to sleep now.

863
00:30:24,550 --> 00:30:25,680
I'll go keep you company tomorrow,

864
00:30:25,680 --> 00:30:26,240
okay?

865
00:30:26,830 --> 00:30:27,440
Sis.

866
00:30:28,070 --> 00:30:28,790
Thank you.

867
00:30:29,550 --> 00:30:30,400
I'm telling the truth.

868
00:30:30,400 --> 00:30:33,000
I, Liu Zhengguang, have no skills
in this life.

869
00:30:33,200 --> 00:30:33,680
I...

870
00:30:33,750 --> 00:30:36,350
But I really haven't suffered
any grievances.

871
00:30:36,720 --> 00:30:39,400
Having friends like you makes it worth it.

872
00:30:39,400 --> 00:30:40,550
Even if tomorrow...

873
00:30:42,110 --> 00:30:42,830
I...

874
00:30:45,270 --> 00:30:46,030
I...

875
00:30:46,750 --> 00:30:48,240
Even if I suddenly drop dead tomorrow,

876
00:30:48,240 --> 00:30:49,200
and I'm gone,

877
00:30:49,200 --> 00:30:50,750
I'd still think it was worth it.

878
00:30:50,750 --> 00:30:52,000
Spit it out.

879
00:30:52,310 --> 00:30:54,040
You can't say things like that.

880
00:30:56,070 --> 00:30:56,960
Just listen to me.

881
00:30:56,960 --> 00:30:57,720
You will definitely

882
00:30:57,720 --> 00:30:59,070
get through this hurdle.

883
00:30:59,070 --> 00:30:59,880
When the time comes,

884
00:30:59,880 --> 00:31:02,140
you'll live to be around a hundred years.

885
00:31:02,350 --> 00:31:03,590
Then we'll find Aunt Ling,

886
00:31:03,590 --> 00:31:04,790
and we'll take her

887
00:31:04,790 --> 00:31:05,720
traveling,

888
00:31:05,880 --> 00:31:07,000
to enjoy life.

889
00:31:25,790 --> 00:31:27,160
Please, please.

890
00:31:28,200 --> 00:31:29,930
Help us find Aunt Ling sooner.

891
00:31:30,030 --> 00:31:30,960
With this little snow,

892
00:31:30,960 --> 00:31:32,350
once the sun comes out tomorrow,

893
00:31:32,350 --> 00:31:33,630
it'll melt by noon.

894
00:31:34,030 --> 00:31:35,110
And this too.

895
00:31:35,550 --> 00:31:36,790
Inaccurate when it should be,

896
00:31:36,790 --> 00:31:38,590
and accurate when it shouldn't.

897
00:31:38,880 --> 00:31:41,630
[Weather forecast]

898
00:31:43,880 --> 00:31:44,440
Then I can only use

899
00:31:44,440 --> 00:31:45,680
my childhood method.

900
00:31:46,640 --> 00:31:48,960
You should be staying at the hospital now,

901
00:31:48,960 --> 00:31:50,550
keeping Zhengguang company.

902
00:31:50,550 --> 00:31:51,920
He doesn't need my company.

903
00:31:51,920 --> 00:31:53,000
We despise each other.

904
00:31:52,800 --> 00:31:56,420
[Fucheng]

905
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:54,240
Can't you provide your brother

906
00:31:54,240 --> 00:31:55,920
with some emotional value?

907
00:31:56,830 --> 00:31:58,440
You've done everything,
but you don't express it.

908
00:31:58,440 --> 00:31:58,830
Aren't you going to stay

909
00:31:58,830 --> 00:32:00,200
at Xiaoximen soon?

910
00:32:00,200 --> 00:32:01,790
Who said I'm going to stay at Xiaoximen?

911
00:32:01,790 --> 00:32:03,070
Haven't you signed the contract?

912
00:32:03,070 --> 00:32:04,270
So what if I signed it?

913
00:32:04,400 --> 00:32:06,060
I'll leave after the surgery.

914
00:32:06,640 --> 00:32:08,770
At worst, I'll pay more compensation.

915
00:32:13,070 --> 00:32:14,730
What about tomorrow morning?

916
00:32:17,680 --> 00:32:19,340
I'm counting on you tomorrow.

917
00:32:20,110 --> 00:32:22,720
Don't let me see any snow.

918
00:32:23,110 --> 00:32:25,590
Don't worry, it's all arranged.

919
00:32:25,680 --> 00:32:27,880
Everything is under control.

920
00:32:36,640 --> 00:32:37,440
Is this what you meant by

921
00:32:37,440 --> 00:32:38,400
everything is under control?

922
00:32:38,400 --> 00:32:39,880
I had everything under control.

923
00:32:39,880 --> 00:32:40,640
I called a car.

924
00:32:40,640 --> 00:32:41,920
But he canceled the order.

925
00:32:41,920 --> 00:32:42,960
What do you have under control?

926
00:32:42,960 --> 00:32:44,200
Why didn't you check in advance?

927
00:32:44,200 --> 00:32:45,070
Look at the time.

928
00:32:45,070 --> 00:32:45,830
Don't panic yet.

929
00:32:45,830 --> 00:32:47,070
I'm more anxious than you, okay?

930
00:32:47,070 --> 00:32:47,720
How can I not be anxious?

931
00:32:47,720 --> 00:32:48,590
With such heavy snow,

932
00:32:48,590 --> 00:32:49,480
can we even get a car?

933
00:32:49,480 --> 00:32:51,200
We can get a car. Trust me!

934
00:32:51,200 --> 00:32:51,790
Trust me!

935
00:32:51,790 --> 00:32:53,350
If not, I'll call my buddy

936
00:32:53,350 --> 00:32:54,070
and ask him to pick us up.

937
00:32:54,070 --> 00:32:54,680
Call him right now!

938
00:32:54,680 --> 00:32:55,740
Call him right now!

939
00:32:56,920 --> 00:32:57,350
Wait a minute.

940
00:32:57,350 --> 00:32:58,200
Here comes one.

941
00:32:58,200 --> 00:32:59,790
I'll hail this one. This one...

942
00:32:59,790 --> 00:33:00,590
Where are you going?

943
00:33:00,590 --> 00:33:01,120
Don't...

944
00:33:03,640 --> 00:33:05,400
Sir, can you go to Xiaoximen?

945
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:05,790
Go, go, go.

946
00:33:05,790 --> 00:33:06,830
Wait for me a moment!

947
00:33:06,830 --> 00:33:07,310
Okay.

948
00:33:09,350 --> 00:33:10,440
-Let’s go. Get off.
-What car?

949
00:33:10,440 --> 00:33:11,200
A tuk-tuk. Hurry up.

950
00:33:11,200 --> 00:33:12,270
A... A tuk-tuk?

951
00:33:13,750 --> 00:33:14,160
Let's go.

952
00:33:14,160 --> 00:33:15,160
The snow is blowing in.

953
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:16,200
There's no time.

954
00:33:16,200 --> 00:33:16,960
I won't take a tuk-tuk.

955
00:33:16,960 --> 00:33:17,160
They don't follow traffic rules.

956
00:33:17,160 --> 00:33:17,790
You're a grown adult.

957
00:33:17,790 --> 00:33:18,720
I can't carry you.

958
00:33:18,720 --> 00:33:19,720
Hurry, hurry, hurry.

959
00:33:19,720 --> 00:33:20,680
Let's go.

960
00:33:23,680 --> 00:33:24,270
Hurry.

961
00:33:24,270 --> 00:33:24,960
Wait a minute.

962
00:33:24,960 --> 00:33:26,420
I'll open the door for you.

963
00:33:26,680 --> 00:33:27,680
Get in.

964
00:33:28,510 --> 00:33:30,550
To Xiaoximen. Full speed ahead.

965
00:33:30,880 --> 00:33:31,720
Alright.

966
00:33:51,510 --> 00:33:52,440
Don't move.

967
00:33:52,640 --> 00:33:53,590
I'm... I'm not moving.

968
00:33:53,590 --> 00:33:54,520
Don't be afraid.

969
00:33:54,550 --> 00:33:55,880
I bought a hat for you.

970
00:33:55,880 --> 00:33:58,310
You can wear it when it's done.

971
00:33:59,440 --> 00:34:00,640
I'm not afraid at all.

972
00:34:05,920 --> 00:34:06,850
Are we there yet?

973
00:34:07,070 --> 00:34:08,550
Almost there. Almost.

974
00:34:10,400 --> 00:34:12,070
Hold tight. We're turning.

975
00:34:18,510 --> 00:34:19,280
We're here.

976
00:34:19,280 --> 00:34:20,190
-Are we?
-Yes.

977
00:34:20,190 --> 00:34:20,850
Be careful.

978
00:34:21,030 --> 00:34:21,760
Sir, how much is it?

979
00:34:21,760 --> 00:34:22,290
Fifteen.

980
00:34:22,790 --> 00:34:23,280
Chen Junnan.

981
00:34:23,280 --> 00:34:25,810
-Keep the change. Let’s go.
-Okay, thank you.

982
00:34:29,800 --> 00:34:31,000
He is both the chief surgeon

983
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:32,320
and the patient's family member.

984
00:34:32,320 --> 00:34:33,280
Make sure he signs

985
00:34:33,280 --> 00:34:35,210
all the relevant documents later.

986
00:34:36,260 --> 00:34:37,920
[Treating patients with skill
and compassion]

987
00:34:37,980 --> 00:34:44,620
[Outpatient Hall]

988
00:34:39,030 --> 00:34:40,290
I can't have snow on me.

989
00:34:41,800 --> 00:34:42,400
It's okay.

990
00:35:26,920 --> 00:35:27,590
Move over.

991
00:35:43,590 --> 00:35:45,120
Come on, give me the marker.

992
00:35:47,070 --> 00:35:47,800
Don't move.

993
00:35:47,920 --> 00:35:49,250
I'll mark the incision.

994
00:35:53,590 --> 00:35:55,050
Turn your head to the side.

995
00:36:01,840 --> 00:36:02,590
Brother.

996
00:36:04,880 --> 00:36:05,940
I don't want to die.

997
00:36:06,190 --> 00:36:07,190
You won't die.

998
00:36:09,760 --> 00:36:10,820
Let's pinky swear.

999
00:36:10,920 --> 00:36:12,380
Keep your dirty hand away.

1000
00:36:16,420 --> 00:36:19,790
[Surgery Status Update]

1001
00:36:21,480 --> 00:36:23,100
[Liu Zhengguang; In Surgery;
Neurosurgery; Bed 6]

1002
00:36:26,990 --> 00:36:30,070
[Operating Room]

1003
00:36:27,070 --> 00:36:28,200
Sit for a while, sis.

1004
00:36:41,760 --> 00:36:42,550
Scalp clip.

1005
00:36:56,510 --> 00:36:58,240
Prepare to open the dura mater.

1006
00:37:06,360 --> 00:37:07,320
Anesthesiologist.

1007
00:37:07,320 --> 00:37:08,920
Prepare to wake the patient.

1008
00:37:10,920 --> 00:37:13,070
[Quiet Please; Authorized Personnel Only]

1009
00:37:15,230 --> 00:37:16,160
Liu Zhengguang,

1010
00:37:16,880 --> 00:37:18,360
can you hear me?

1011
00:37:19,440 --> 00:37:20,230
Liu Zhengguang,

1012
00:37:20,230 --> 00:37:21,510
answer if you hear us.

1013
00:37:24,710 --> 00:37:25,640
Liu Zhengguang!

1014
00:37:25,960 --> 00:37:26,800
I hear you.

1015
00:37:29,480 --> 00:37:31,030
To ensure your language abilities

1016
00:37:31,030 --> 00:37:32,030
aren't affected,

1017
00:37:32,480 --> 00:37:33,280
for the next part,

1018
00:37:33,280 --> 00:37:33,920
I need you

1019
00:37:33,920 --> 00:37:35,030
to cooperate with me

1020
00:37:35,030 --> 00:37:36,160
while you are awake.

1021
00:37:37,030 --> 00:37:39,030
Prepare to start the language test.

1022
00:37:41,190 --> 00:37:42,150
Now,

1023
00:37:42,230 --> 00:37:44,760
try counting from one.

1024
00:37:46,400 --> 00:37:47,000
One.

1025
00:37:48,400 --> 00:37:48,920
Two.

1026
00:37:49,920 --> 00:37:50,800
Three.

1027
00:37:51,510 --> 00:37:52,670
Four...

1028
00:37:54,190 --> 00:37:55,190
Give me the label.

1029
00:37:57,710 --> 00:37:59,400
Count a bit slower, Liu Zhengguang.

1030
00:37:59,400 --> 00:38:00,190
Four.

1031
00:38:01,360 --> 00:38:02,150
Five.

1032
00:38:02,630 --> 00:38:03,510
Count slower.

1033
00:38:04,920 --> 00:38:05,710
Six.

1034
00:38:06,480 --> 00:38:07,630
Seven...

1035
00:38:10,320 --> 00:38:11,180
Come on, label.

1036
00:38:15,030 --> 00:38:15,800
Cotton pad.

1037
00:38:16,760 --> 00:38:17,670
Is my

1038
00:38:18,030 --> 00:38:19,400
head

1039
00:38:19,480 --> 00:38:22,110
open right now?

1040
00:38:22,480 --> 00:38:23,280
Yes.

1041
00:38:23,550 --> 00:38:24,800
But don't worry.

1042
00:38:24,920 --> 00:38:26,760
The surgery is going very smoothly.

1043
00:38:26,760 --> 00:38:27,940
I guess

1044
00:38:29,550 --> 00:38:31,140
I'm speaking

1045
00:38:31,960 --> 00:38:34,190
with an open mind now.

1046
00:38:37,320 --> 00:38:39,050
Can two people with type O blood

1047
00:38:40,230 --> 00:38:41,480
have

1048
00:38:42,630 --> 00:38:44,400
a child with type A blood?

1049
00:38:46,280 --> 00:38:47,210
What do you mean?

1050
00:38:47,480 --> 00:38:48,840
C-Can you repeat that?

1051
00:38:48,840 --> 00:38:49,670
I understand.

1052
00:38:50,510 --> 00:38:52,360
So this is your so-called

1053
00:38:52,360 --> 00:38:53,440
scientific proof?

1054
00:38:53,800 --> 00:38:54,760
My

1055
00:38:55,960 --> 00:38:57,880
parents both have

1056
00:38:59,280 --> 00:39:00,280
type O blood.

1057
00:39:04,230 --> 00:39:05,760
I have type A blood.

1058
00:39:07,440 --> 00:39:09,190
I checked online.

1059
00:39:09,280 --> 00:39:11,590
This is completely impossible.

1060
00:39:11,590 --> 00:39:13,000
Nothing is absolute.

1061
00:39:13,070 --> 00:39:14,840
Maybe the blood type
was displayed incorrectly.

1062
00:39:14,840 --> 00:39:15,710
What if there's a

1063
00:39:15,710 --> 00:39:17,030
one in tens of thousands chance

1064
00:39:17,030 --> 00:39:18,290
of a genetic mutation,

1065
00:39:18,710 --> 00:39:19,800
and two type O parents

1066
00:39:19,800 --> 00:39:21,330
end up having a type A child?

1067
00:39:22,110 --> 00:39:23,550
Stop fooling me.

1068
00:39:23,880 --> 00:39:26,000
It's possible. I can testify.

1069
00:39:26,550 --> 00:39:27,400
What do you mean?

1070
00:39:27,400 --> 00:39:28,550
I... I... I...

1071
00:39:28,550 --> 00:39:30,110
I mu... mutated?

1072
00:39:30,110 --> 00:39:31,770
Alright, don't overthink it.

1073
00:39:31,800 --> 00:39:32,840
Get some more sleep.

1074
00:39:32,840 --> 00:39:34,300
I'll take care of the rest.

1075
00:39:43,510 --> 00:39:46,170
Prepare to resect
the malformed blood vessels.

1076
00:39:49,930 --> 00:39:50,450
Dr. Liu.

1077
00:39:50,480 --> 00:39:51,400
The patient's blood pressure is dropping.

1078
00:39:51,400 --> 00:39:52,320
70 over 40.

1079
00:40:01,550 --> 00:40:03,360
Massive bleeding
from the malformed vessels.

1080
00:40:03,360 --> 00:40:05,140
Administer norepinephrine.

1081
00:40:05,360 --> 00:40:06,960
Get 2 units of red blood cells

1082
00:40:06,960 --> 00:40:08,190
and 400 ml of plasma.

1083
00:40:09,720 --> 00:40:11,440
Stabilize the heart rate at around 80.

1084
00:40:11,440 --> 00:40:13,040
Give me a hemostatic sponge.

1085
00:40:16,000 --> 00:40:17,460
Give me hemostatic gauze.

1086
00:40:20,840 --> 00:40:21,630
Cotton pads.

1087
00:40:23,320 --> 00:40:24,720
Give me an aneurysm clip.

1088
00:40:41,470 --> 00:40:46,210
[No smoking]

1089
00:41:05,510 --> 00:41:06,760
Old Tower.

1090
00:41:07,630 --> 00:41:09,340
Please bless my brother.

1091
00:41:09,510 --> 00:41:11,110
May he never be afraid of snow again,

1092
00:41:11,110 --> 00:41:13,670
and stay home to play with me from now on.

1093
00:41:31,200 --> 00:41:34,100
[Starry Night] [Prosperous Dynasty]

1094
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:34,330
I'm telling you, Zhuzi.

1095
00:41:34,510 --> 00:41:36,000
You could never imagine such a scene

1096
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:37,110
in your entire life.

1097
00:41:37,110 --> 00:41:37,840
Right?

1098
00:41:37,840 --> 00:41:39,370
The head was cut right open.

1099
00:41:46,280 --> 00:41:48,110
Looking like a Martian.

1100
00:41:48,230 --> 00:41:50,090
Wait, how did you see it yourself?

1101
00:41:50,230 --> 00:41:51,280
I imagined it.

1102
00:41:52,360 --> 00:41:54,320
The most important thing
is that's not the point.

1103
00:41:54,320 --> 00:41:55,030
Sis.

1104
00:41:55,320 --> 00:41:57,670
The point is I was talking
and laughing cheerfully.

1105
00:41:57,670 --> 00:41:58,880
I was not scared at all.

1106
00:41:58,880 --> 00:41:59,880
That was awesome.

1107
00:41:59,880 --> 00:42:00,480
Really?

1108
00:42:00,800 --> 00:42:02,190
How come I remember
the day before yesterday,

1109
00:42:02,190 --> 00:42:03,720
you almost peed your pants?

1110
00:42:04,630 --> 00:42:07,090
Liu Zhengliang is always contradicting me.

1111
00:42:12,920 --> 00:42:13,840
What's wrong?

1112
00:42:17,030 --> 00:42:18,110
See for yourself.

1113
00:42:19,110 --> 00:42:20,770
You didn't mess me up, did you?

1114
00:42:22,030 --> 00:42:22,840
Zhuzi,

1115
00:42:22,840 --> 00:42:24,370
crank the bed up a bit for me.

1116
00:42:29,740 --> 00:42:32,670
[Kinship Test Report]

1117
00:42:30,170 --> 00:42:30,840
The blood

1118
00:42:30,840 --> 00:42:32,510
was drawn
during your physical examination.

1119
00:42:32,510 --> 00:42:34,230
The test results just came in.

1120
00:42:36,670 --> 00:42:37,710
What a pity.

1121
00:42:38,280 --> 00:42:39,920
Although the IQ gap between us

1122
00:42:39,920 --> 00:42:40,670
makes it look like we're not

1123
00:42:40,670 --> 00:42:41,710
the same species,

1124
00:42:42,190 --> 00:42:42,760
we are actually

1125
00:42:42,760 --> 00:42:44,280
biological brothers.

1126
00:42:46,150 --> 00:42:47,480
I was happy for nothing.

1127
00:42:48,320 --> 00:42:49,960
It's really a shame.

1128
00:42:51,550 --> 00:42:52,960
Such a shame!

1129
00:43:02,110 --> 00:43:03,510
What's the shame in that?

1130
00:43:08,630 --> 00:43:09,760
It's authentic.
